sesmesh in US-SOMO
==================

This directory holds sesmesh, a mesher for the solvent-excluded surface (SES) of a
set of spheres, from https://github.com/ehb54/sesmesh at commit a01ff94 (2026-11-13,
"Merge pull request #2 from ehb54/phase4").  The files are unchanged.

  src/          the sesmesh sources: ses, mesh, clean, io, parallel, vec3, and
                sesmesh.cpp, the command-line program
  README.md     sesmesh's README: method, options and validation
  LICENSE       sesmesh's MIT license

sesmesh is MIT-licensed (see LICENSE), so it can be built into US-SOMO.


How SOMO builds and uses it
---------------------------

libus_somo.pro compiles src/{ses,mesh,clean,io,parallel}.cpp into the library.
src/sesmesh.cpp (the program's main) is kept only to mirror sesmesh's tree.  SOMO
includes the headers by path ("../sesmesh/src/ses.h"); src/ is not on the include
path, because src/io.h would hide the system <io.h> on Windows.  sesmesh needs C++14
or later, so libus_somo.pro sets CONFIG += c++17.

When "Compute on the solvent-excluded surface of the bead model" is checked in the
ZENO options, US_Hydrodyn_Zeno::run (src/us_hydrodyn_zeno.cpp) takes the bead
centres and radii as the spheres, meshes their SES with the probe radius and grid
spacing set there (cleaned up, cavities filled, unless unchecked), and writes the
triangles to the .bod file as TRIANGLE lines instead of one SPHERE line per bead.
sesmesh runs on as many threads as ZENO (SOMO's thread setting).


Updating
--------

Copy src/*.{h,cpp}, README.md and LICENSE from a newer sesmesh commit, update the
commit above, and check that the file list in libus_somo.pro still matches src/.
